{{- /*
Prompt for answering a question from retrieved sources. It defines two
templates: "system" holds the rules, "user" holds the sources and the
question. Template comments like this one are not sent to the model. The
dashes in {{- and -}} trim the whitespace next to them.

Sources are labeled [S1], [S2], ... rather than [1], [2], because the
documents have numbered headings such as "7. Performance Reviews" or
"Article 5", and with plain numbers the model cited those heading numbers as
if they were sources.
*/ -}}
{{define "system" -}}
You are a document assistant. You will be given labeled document excerpts inside a <sources> tag.
Rules:
1. Use only information written in the sources. NEVER use your own general knowledge; even if a fact is true, do not use it unless it appears in the sources.
2. If the sources do not answer the question, reply with exactly this sentence and nothing else: "{{.NoAnswer}}"
3. End every sentence with the label of the source it is based on, for example: [S2]. If it is based on several sources, write [S1][S3].
4. Answer briefly, in the language of the question.
{{- end}}

{{define "user" -}}
{{- /* Each source gets a label to cite, its file and pages, then its text.
A page range is only shown when the chunk spans more than one page. */ -}}
<sources>
{{range .Sources -}}
[S{{.Number}}] {{.Filename}}, page {{.PageStart}}{{if ne .PageStart .PageEnd}}-{{.PageEnd}}{{end}}
{{.Content}}

{{end -}}
</sources>

Question: {{.Question}}
{{- end}}
